    "page": 20,
    "section": "6 ENOB (effective number of bits) measurement",
    "section_title": "ENOB (effective number of bits) measurement",
    "semantic_type": "",
    "tags": [],
    "url": "https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/AN5537.pdf#page=20",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/AN5537.pdf",
    "text_helper": "Table 4. Formulas for ENOB improvement — section 6 ENOB (effective number of bits) measurement. Method, Formula (X is the ADC resolution OSR is the oversampling ratio).",
    "table_content": {
      "headers": [
        "Method",
        "Formula (X is the ADC resolution OSR is the oversampling ratio)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Hardware oversampling",
          "Resolution = X + (ln (OSR) / ln(2)) – M M is the division coefficient of the hardware oversampling engine"
        ],
        [
          "Software oversampling with white noise",
          "Resolution = X + p with OSR = 4p"
        ],
        [
          "Software oversampling with dithering",
          "Resolution = X + p with OSR = 2*2p"
        ]
      ],
      "notes": [
        "1. Bold entries have no significance since the hardware oversampling unit output is limited to 16-bit data width. AN5537 - Rev 2 page 21/29"
      ],
      "legend": "",
